  "id": "childhood-absence-epilepsy",
  "term": "childhood absence epilepsy",
  "definition": "Childhood absence epilepsy is a childhood epilepsy in which cognitive difficulties may remain even after seizures are brought under control. In particular, problems with attention and executive functioning can persist and contribute to school difficulties.",
